1
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:07,360
I have seen this pin on Agent J twice.

2
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,400
Once in Ngai Ka-yan's office.

3
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,520
Is it related to Ngai Ka-yan's death?

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,680
What does this logo stand for?

5
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,640
You have seen this logo before?

6
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,600
Three months ago, after Ngai Ka-yan died,

7
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,160
I arranged a program on TV.

8
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:29,880
(One week after the incident)

9
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,280
I put the online channel staff on the show

10
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,640
to see if we'll find any new leads.

11
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,960
Why do you have a script?

12
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:38,040
Netizens criticized Jarvis,

13
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,280
I must defend him.

14
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,680
Watch what you say, don't make things worse.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,160
Welcome to Healthy Souls.

16
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,040
The recent talk of the town is definitely

17
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:51,480
the livestreaming of the murder
on J Weekly.

18
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:52,880
A lot of people claimed to be

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,960
emotionally distressed after watching
the livecast.

20
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:59,360
Today, we have with us Miss Wong,
a clinical psychologist,

21
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,880
Miss Ho, an educational psychologist,

22
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,560
Helen, the co-sponsor of the livecast

23
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,840
and Wendy and Paul from the online channel

24
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:05,720
to have a chat with us.

25
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,080
The image of Jarvis dropping to the floor
after he inhaled the oxygen

26
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:10,280
is still fresh on my mind.

27
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:12,800
Wendy's condition is very common.

28
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,800
With the advanced information technology,

29
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:18,000
people like to save videos and
send them out.

30
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:22,440
I'd like to appeal to everyone to stop it

31
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,920
and stop watching it again.

32
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:27,040
Repeated viewing will only increase
your emotional distress.

33
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:30,880
I want to say Jarvis was very talented.

34
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:33,680
He only wanted to bring people joy.

35
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:37,040
Unfortunately, he died in an accident.

36
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:40,880
Her reaction tells me she's a fan.

37
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:44,280
In recent years, it's common to make
videos of people playing tricks on others.

38
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,640
It's a hit among young people.

39
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,360
Miss Ho, what's your view on this trend?

40
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:53,920
Young people think pranks are harmless

41
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,280
and they trick each other.

42
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:58,840
Over time, they tend to make light
of the danger involved.

43
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,240
If we don't correct this mentality in time,

44
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:05,920
when they get older, it'll easily cause
serious consequences.

45
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,680
Hey, watch it!

46
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,440
Jarvis wanted us to deal with
the absurd with laughter.

47
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,880
His videos helped me get back on my feet.

48
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:16,640
She's a die-hard fan, not an ordinary fan.

49
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:20,160
Wendy was right.

50
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,560
Jarvis had good intentions.

51
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:26,560
But honestly, he often crossed the line.

52
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,200
That's why our channel will work with
the Rehab Club

53
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,840
to provide support to viewers
who were affected.

54
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:35,760
Paul is more sensible.

55
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,640
We'll set up an Emotional Support Group,

56
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,120
you're all welcome to join us.

57
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,720
Lok Hiu-sin never went to
the online channel.

58
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:45,160
We can rule her out.

59
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,280
When you make a video of a prank,

60
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,720
it's likely to cause physical harm or
even death,

61
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,600
to both the prankster and the victim.

62
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,520
It is also likely to traumatize those
who watched the video.

63
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,840
If anyone is emotionally distressed,

64
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:03,040
I suggest you consult a
clinical psychologist

65
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,360
It's this pattern again.

66
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,280
Why does she have a bracelet like that?

67
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:12,480
Gogo Sir, thanks for your suggestion,

68
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:15,360
or we wouldn't have consulted experts
to deal with the aftermath on TV.

69
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,640
Don't mention it.

70
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:20,280
Paul, will you continue to run the channel?

71
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:22,800
Miss Lok, can I ask you about this bracelet?

72
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:26,320
Helen! Didn't get a chance to talk earlier.

73
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,080
Are you busy? Let's have lunch.

74
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:28,840
Great!

75
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,640
You know each other?

76
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,080
Miss Ho was my counselor in high school.

77
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:36,000
She was a great help after my accident.

78
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:37,360
Sorry!

79
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:39,760
Let's go.

80
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,360
Hello, Ching Sir?

81
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,080
Gogo, I need you to check on something.

82
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,680
Come back to the Police station.

83
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:46,880
Yes, Sir!

84
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:54,720
It's been a while since I visited you
at school.

85
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:58,480
I didn't expect us to meet
under such circumstances.

86
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:01,640
I haven't seen Ngai Ka-yan for
so many years.

87
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:03,360
I can't believe when I hear about him again,

88
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,800
it was about his death.

89
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:09,640
Helen, when we were on air just now,

90
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,600
I noticed you were very nervous.

91
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,080
Are you upset?

92
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:16,640
No.

93
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:19,040
The livestreaming of the
Static Apnea Challenge

94
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,960
was a joint project by your Club
and the online channel.

95
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:22,200
Now that someone is dead,

96
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,320
you feel bad about it?

97
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:28,160
(Eight years ago)

98
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:42,960
Thanks.

99
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,400
Hey!

100
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,040
You're here. Good, practice with me.

101
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,400
Practice? Exams are coming up.

102
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,360
I'm not smart like you.

103
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,400
I need to study.

104
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,400
You spent too much time playing
video games.

105
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,920
Cramming in the last minute won't help.

106
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:04,200
I'm trying out for the Hong Kong Team
next week.

107
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,360
You'll be the goalie for me.

108
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,160
Again?

109
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:10,840
How about...I'll kiss you each time
you block the ball.

110
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,520
Right away!

111
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:37,280
Last one...if you fail, you'll get nothing.

112
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:38,720
Bring it on!

113
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:52,080
Even if I fail, you must kiss me.

114
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,120
Just once. I blocked many shots.

115
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,080
No!
Just once...

116
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,880
No, you didn't!

117
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,080
That's my bottle!

118
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,200
Your mouth touched my saliva,

119
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,400
that's an indirect kiss.

120
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:09,760
That's childish! You're not in grade school.

121
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,760
I wish we had met in grade school.

122
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,640
Then we could be childhood sweethearts.

123
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,760
Did you know ordinary water
has no electrolyte?

124
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,680
I'll get you something with electrolyte.

125
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,040
I'll go with you.

126
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,880
I also need to run to the toilet.

127
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,600
Are you OK?

128
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,200
Get up...
No...

129
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,800
Where are you hurt?
My back...

130
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,800
(0 Cycle Drain)

131
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,760
Ready for your housewarming present?

132
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,760
Aren't we moving together?

133
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,960
Is the present for me or for yourself?

134
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,480
Just take a look.

135
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:23,920
I'm unveiling it...

136
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,520
Most people put up a starry sky,

137
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,640
why do we have the Hong Kong map?

138
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,000
Remember this place?

139
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,760
It's where we went on our first date.

140
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,520
Of course I remember.

141
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:42,320
Others go shopping, see a movie
or eat out on a date.

142
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,880
We're out in the boonies.

143
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:48,000
If I ask other people to go to
the Geopark with me,

144
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,280
they'll say I'm a bore.

145
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:53,280
Only you would go anywhere with me,

146
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,720
no matter how far away it is.

147
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,560
You know it's boring too?

148
00:08:57,480 --> 00:09:00,000
Your dream is to become a geologist.

149
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:02,160
Of course I'd help you realize your dream.

150
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,000
Too bad I can't walk

151
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,800
and I can't go to Yellowstone Park with you.

152
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,160
Silly.

153
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:13,680
I'm just happy enjoying the breeze
at Wong Shek Pier.

154
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,440
Though I can't walk,

155
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:20,880
I can still go places with you.

156
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:25,280
Then I'm giving you this Hong Kong map.

157
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:26,560
(Eight years later)

158
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:29,920
When you're bored during your dialysis
at night,

159
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:31,520
you can look at it to kill time.

160
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,680
Let me help you.

161
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,160
No, I can manage.

162
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:48,960
Your clothes are here...

163
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:53,680
I'm going to the US next week.

164
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,320
I probably won't be back anytime soon.

165
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:02,400
Send me loads of pictures.

166
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:06,400
You plan to stay here?

167
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,160
You're not moving back in with Auntie?

168
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:13,280
No. I should learn to be more independent.

169
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,920
I don't want to be anyone's burden.

170
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:20,400
Thanks for looking after me
these past eight years.

171
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,800
You're not a burden to anyone.

172
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:28,160
You're the most important person in my life.

173
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,880
Don't worry about me. Go pursue your dream.

174
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:41,800
It's time for my appointment.

175
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:46,480
Take care.

176
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,760
Hi, Auntie Ching! Long time no see.

177
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:16,920
Well? Same as usual?

178
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,880
Oh...right!

179
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:21,440
I think you're amazing.

180
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,360
You have been buying pork from me
for so long

181
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,880
and you haven't gained an inch.

182
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:28,400
What? Oh, thanks...

183
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,240
Auntie Ching, what's wrong?

184
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,200
You forgot your change!

185
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:35,840
Where's the boyfriend?

186
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:37,360
He didn't come with you?

187
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,720
There's no need to bother him every time.

188
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:42,400
That's true.

189
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:50,400
The report shows your renal failure
is getting worse.

190
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:54,320
I also noticed your ostomy is
slightly infected.

191
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,680
I fell down a while ago.

192
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,080
Your crushing injury eight years ago,

193
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,760
caused muscle fibers to break down

194
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,920
and resulted in rhabdomyolysis and
you require dialysis.

195
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,160
You must be careful with the ostomy.

196
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:09,360
Persistent inflammation may
lead to complications.

197
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:13,920
Dr. Yuen, there's no other treatment?

198
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:16,560
Honestly, medication and dialysis

199
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,400
can only cure the symptoms, not the cause.

200
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,720
I suggest you register for
a kidney transplant.

201
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:34,400
You've been so helpful...here, my treat.

202
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,240
Thanks, Miss Ho.

203
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,000
I'm truly grateful to you

204
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:41,120
for taking time from your busy schedule
to play with SEN kids.

205
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,720
Working at the Rehab Club,

206
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:45,520
I often come across students with
Special Educational Needs.

207
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,360
They need a lot of tender loving care.

208
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:51,040
Yes, that's why you must play with them
more often.

209
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:53,360
They adore a big sister like you.

210
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,040
I will when I have time.

211
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:59,200
Helen, you still have such a
sunny personality.

212
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,040
Even when you have problems of your own,

213
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,280
I saw you had fun with the kids just now.

214
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:08,720
I counselled you for six years

215
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,520
I watched you injured yourself
when you were in Form 6,

216
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:14,240
came back to school and went on to college.

217
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,720
I know exactly what you're thinking.

218
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:22,080
The brighter the sun, the bigger the shadow.

219
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,280
I broke up with Ching.

220
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:29,280
I moved in with my boyfriend a year ago.

221
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,040
We were quite happy.

222
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,480
Sorry, I was late getting off work.

223
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:33,360
Let me help you.

224
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:35,840
No, I can manage. Your work is important.

225
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,680
I know you want to be independent.

226
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:39,600
But this concerns your health.

227
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,720
Let me help you.

228
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,400
(Please wait)

229
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,440
(0 Cycle Drain)

230
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,600
Wait while I prepare dinner.

231
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,960
But as I watched this First Honor
Geology major,

232
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:57,200
who doesn't spend his time doing research,

233
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:00,400
but takes care of me and my dialysis,

234
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,160
it breaks my heart.

235
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:05,120
Hello? I know the results came out.

236
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,920
Yes...I didn't have time to go back
to the office.

237
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,000
OK, I'll follow up tomorrow.

238
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:14,480
OK...thank you...bye!

239
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,560
You really must try this egg.

240
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,800
I seldom make it so perfect. Try it.

241
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:24,320
Remember what day is next week?

242
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:28,160
Our 8th anniversary.

243
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:32,000
Yes. I have everything planned out.

244
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,440
We're not going to Wong Shek Pier.

245
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,640
Then let's go to Yellowstone Park.

246
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:38,480
You want to go away? OK.

247
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,240
But you must wait till
I'm not so busy at work.

248
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,600
No, I'm not waiting for you.

249
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:43,200
And you should stop waiting for me.

250
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:49,120
What's wrong? You're not feeling well?

251
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:53,520
I don't want you to waste your life away
because of me.

252
00:14:56,200 --> 00:15:01,200
Don't be silly...you are my life.

253
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:08,800
I saw the letter from Professor Chan.

254
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:12,240
He pulled some strings for you

255
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:16,400
so you can do research work in the US
for a professor you admire.

256
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,560
Yes, I got a letter from him,

257
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:24,560
but I haven't said yes.

258
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,640
Professor Chan thought I have the
right qualifications,

259
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:28,880
and sent out my CV without asking me.

260
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:29,840
Do you want to go?

261
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:39,760
Ching, your world should be Yellowstone Park

262
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,600
not Wong Shek Pier.

263
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:47,840
But I don't want to leave you.

264
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,520
Go pursue your dream.

265
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,840
So you brought it up?

266
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:56,960
I thought it was just puppy love between you

267
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,880
I never expected it to last this long.

268
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:01,680
If we hadn't been through
thick and thin together,

269
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,520
ours should have been puppy love

270
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,800
and we would have broken up.

271
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:10,400
Your accident was such a major blow to you.

272
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:12,880
I thought it was an accident too,

273
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:15,760
until recently...

274
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,760
On behalf of the Rehab Club,

275
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:20,080
I had a meeting with people from J Weekly.

276
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,200
And I saw him again.

277
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:24,320
Because the livestreaming was a fundraiser,

278
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,000
I had to do my homework

279
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:29,520
and know more about the background
and characteristics of J Weekly.

280
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:33,120
I found one of the older videos
Jarvis made for his channel.

281
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:35,680
I watched it carefully...
Watch it, don't kill yourself!

282
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:39,440
It was identical to what happened to me.

283
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:44,280
At first, I thought I missed a step

284
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,440
and I landed on the ground.

285
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,960
But watching the video of that
fishing line football,

286
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:52,800
it reminded me when I fell,
the football moved away.

287
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,040
It was likely someone pulled it away.

288
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,560
But I was in so much pain I didn't notice.

289
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,440
Are you OK?

290
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,840
Get up...
No...

291
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,320
Where are you hurt?
My back...

292
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:12,560
Before the accident, I saw him
in the playground.

293
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:16,400
It's very likely he was the prankster
who paralyzed me.

294
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,960
He acted on a whim to pull a prank,

295
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,200
you ended up in a wheelchair

296
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:22,640
and needed dialysis.

297
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:26,640
He used to trick people for fun.

298
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:30,600
Then evolved into fishing for likes and
online traffic

299
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,960
and he continued to hurt people.

300
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:36,040
For a bunch of numbers,

301
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:37,920
he got himself killed in the end.

302
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:38,880
Is it worth it?

303
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:52,280
We zeroed in on Tsang Chun-kit and
Hung Tzi-long,

304
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,880
now this Director Tsui came from nowhere.

305
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:57,680
But we have no evidence to link him
to Ngai Ka-yan's death.

306
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,840
On the set of Healthy Souls,

307
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:02,240
I noticed the logo on Lok Hiu-sin's bracelet

308
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:05,360
is identical to the pin found in
Ngai Ka-yan's office.

309
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:09,120
I also noticed Lok Hiu-sin seemed
very uptight during the shoot.

310
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:13,920
Lok Hiu-sin and Ngai Ka-yan
only worked on this fundraiser,

311
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:15,200
why did she kill him?

312
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,200
Wow, this woman is vicious.

313
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:21,640
Her ex-boyfriend betrayed her ten years ago.

314
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,720
She held a grudge,

315
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,440
spent ten years to plan her revenge

316
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:27,080
and killed the ex.

317
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:29,360
Find out how Lok Hiu-sin became paralyzed.

318
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:36,880
Officers, this is Miss Ho.

319
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:37,880
Take your time.

320
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:38,560
Thank you.

321
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:39,200
Right!

322
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,080
Can I help you, Officers?

323
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:46,160
I remember you said on TV,

324
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,120
young people are immature

325
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:50,360
and often overlook the danger of a prank.

326
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:53,080
When they grow up, the consequence
could be unthinkable.

327
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,520
Ngai Ka-yan was one of your students,

328
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:58,240
can you tell us what he was like back then?

329
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,840
Ngai Ka-yan was very naughty

330
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,640
and often pulled pranks on his classmates.

331
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:03,880
We had a lot of complaints about him.

332
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,000
When Ngai Ka-yan was in high school,

333
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,400
he wasn't too popular among
his classmates, right?

334
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:10,560
No, he wasn't.

335
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,200
He wasn't mean or anything.

336
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:15,760
His pranks were quite harmless.

337
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:18,640
Did his harmless pranks

338
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:21,200
ever lead to anything disastrous?

339
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:24,880
Yes, someone got hurt.

340
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,200
Was it Lok Hiu-sin?

341
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:34,880
Are you suggesting Helen is involved
in Ngai Ka-yan's case?

342
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,800
Just answer my question.

343
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:42,480
All I can say is that,
Helen has a kind heart.

344
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:45,880
She would never intentionally hurt anyone.

345
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,560
Regarding your questions,

346
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,560
because they involve my students' privacy,

347
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:51,840
I'm sorry I can't disclose anything.

348
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:56,320
Miss Ho has such a tight trap.

349
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,320
That's not what I think.

350
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:02,040
Miss Ho's reaction already told me
we're on the right track.

351
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:05,560
Lok Hiu-sin is paralyzed because
of Ngai Ka-yan.

352
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,360
I can't believe they went to
the same high school,

353
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,840
just different grades.

354
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:13,440
Lok Hiu-sin was an outstanding athlete
with good prospects.

355
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:16,600
She's now paralyzed because of
Ngai Ka-yan's prank.

356
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:19,600
Revenge was her motive to kill him.

357
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:22,800
But she never went to the channel

358
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,560
and she wasn't at the scene
during the livestreaming.

359
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,960
Maybe someone at the channel
is her accomplice.

360
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:31,200
Gogo Sir, let's bring her in
for questioning.

361
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,160
Not yet. If she had an accomplice,

362
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:37,280
this person must have a close
relationship with her.

363
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,760
Shopping?
Hi, how are you?

364
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:41,880
Boss!

365
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:44,800
Hi! Lean pork and pig knuckles for you.

366
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,520
Thank you.

367
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:47,640
Well? How are you going to cook
your pork knuckles?

368
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,880
I'm just getting them for a friend
from the Rehab Club.

369
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,040
I see.

370
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:52,960
Sin!

371
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:54,000
Mom!

372
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,120
Auntie Ching?

373
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,280
I bought a chicken.

374
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:00,120
Pork and chicken are both high in protein.

375
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:02,040
Your skin will be silky soft.

376
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:04,240
You're such a sweet talker.

377
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:07,200
I don't know why either,
I'm always happy to see her.

378
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:09,760
My daughter takes after me.

379
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:15,760
Way back when, I was Ms. Sunshine in
Tai Hom Village and San Po Kong.

380
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,560
They appear to be mother and daughter.

381
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,280
If they're mother and daughter

382
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,120
then Lok Hiu-sin has a motive for murder.

383
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:23,680
Maybe they plotted Ngai Kan-yan's murder.

384
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:30,160
What's the occasion? Why the extra dishes?

385
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:32,280
Today is my last day.

386
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:36,160
Since I can finally take a break
after working for so long,

387
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:39,360
I thought we should celebrate.

388
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:42,400
But you sound so sad.

389
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,040
Still thinking about Jarvis?

390
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:50,000
No, I stopped thinking about it. It's over.

391
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:53,200
You should too.

392
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,240
The key is to get well.

393
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,600
I know.

394
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:13,120
We assumed Auntie Ching had no motive.

395
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:16,040
But now we know she's Lok Hiu-sin's mother

396
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:18,720
and there's such a grudge between
Lok Hiu-sin and Ngai Ka-yan.

397
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:21,440
But Auntie Ching worked for the
online channel for so many years,

398
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,280
she wouldn't need to wait this long
to make a move.

399
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:28,880
Maybe Lok Hiu-sin ran into Ngai Ka-yan
only because of the recent fundraiser,

400
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,600
and just found out he paralyzed her.

401
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:36,960
If Auntie Ching knew
she worked for the enemy for so long,

402
00:22:37,600 --> 00:22:39,280
she's likely to fall apart.

403
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:43,200
A grassroot working mom with a pretty
and capable daughter

404
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:45,440
who found out someone paralyzed
her daughter,

405
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:47,360
can't possibly pretend nothing happened.

406
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,920
How did Auntie Ching do it?

407
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:53,880
She was at the office of the channel
at lunch time.

408
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:57,040
She claimed she was in the pantry
with her headphone on

409
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,600
and didn't know when the vase was broken.

410
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:02,280
During that time frame,
no one really knew her exact location.

411
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:04,800
She could have gone into Ngai Ka-yan's
office to swap the cylinder

412
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:06,360
and accidentally knocked over the vase.

413
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:09,640
During the livestreaming,
Auntie Ching was not at the pool,

414
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:10,960
she had the perfect alibi

415
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:12,800
and can frame Tom and Paul.

416
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,200
Ko Sir, what does a cleaning lady

417
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:17,840
know about H2S, hydrogen sulfide?

418
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:19,360
We're talking about making poisonous gas.

419
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,520
Brother Cheong, don't forget,

420
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:23,440
her daughter is an A student in science.

421
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,920
Anyone who knows about the danger
of swamp gas

422
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,360
would know what hydrogen sulfide is.

423
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,440
You're saying Auntie Ching acted alone

424
00:23:29,520 --> 00:23:30,720
and Helen is her accomplice?

425
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:33,120
Right now, the key is to find out

426
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:35,200
how they got their hands on the H2S,

427
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,640
then we can prove they're the killers.

428
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,640
Maybe like Tom and Paul,

429
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:41,040
DIY in a factory building?

430
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:44,280
(Government Laboratory)

431
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,600
Please come this way.

432
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:51,040
These are stink bombs.

433
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:53,320
And this is the one you want to see most,

434
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:55,280
a high concentration of H2S.

435
00:23:55,760 --> 00:23:56,400
Thanks.

436
00:23:58,560 --> 00:24:00,640
Check the manufacturer of
the gas cylinder.

437
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,080
Find out where they sold this lot.

438
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,280
(University Lab)

439
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:05,320
Ko Sir, Lee Sir, when we got your inquiry,

440
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:07,080
we started checking

441
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:11,080
and found out your gas cylinder
came from our lab.

442
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:13,640
Why so many?

443
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,200
From different manufacturers.

444
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:17,560
These are all highly concentrated H2S.

445
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:21,320
This is the one in the picture you sent us.

446
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:27,120
I guess your tight security

447
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:29,280
can prevent people from wandering around?

448
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:30,400
You're quite right.

449
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:34,160
That's why we don't usually count
our gas cylinders.

450
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:35,680
Has anything been missing lately?

451
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:38,800
We took stock after we got your call,

452
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:40,880
five cylinders of H2S are missing.

453
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,360
Can you show my colleague your CCTV?

454
00:24:43,640 --> 00:24:45,800
I want to know if anyone suspicious
was lurking around the lab.

455
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,360
I also need a roster of your lab staff.

456
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:55,120
Gogo Sir, CCTV showed no forced entry.

457
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,840
Security also double checked,

458
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:58,160
there was no sign of burglary.

459
00:24:58,280 --> 00:25:00,160
It's probably an inside job.

460
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:03,280
Well? You found anything on the roster?

461
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,640
Auntie Ching is not on the cleaning staff.

462
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:08,280
Lok Hiu-sin is also not on the list.

463
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:10,080
What about staff from the online channel?

464
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:11,080
Nope.

465
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:15,360
Another dead end. I thought we'd find
new leads.

466
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:20,160
Ginseng chicken smells great.
I'm so blessed.

467
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:23,120
I haven't seen this look in a long time.

468
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:26,160
I just had dinner with you two weeks ago.

469
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:29,280
But it wasn't just us.

470
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:31,800
He was here the whole time...

471
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:36,000
I'll be home for dinner more often.

472
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:38,840
I better stock up on meal replacements.

473
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:42,160
The way you feed me, I'll gain weight.

474
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:46,000
I'll think about what to cook for you.

475
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,840
None of this would be a burden
to your kidneys.

476
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:50,040
This is great.

477
00:25:51,080 --> 00:25:53,680
You just went to your follow-up appointment,

478
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:54,880
what did the doctor say?

479
00:25:57,720 --> 00:26:01,920
What's wrong? You seem preoccupied.

480
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:03,280
Nothing.

481
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:06,880
What are you not telling me? Say it.

482
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:10,960
Nothing.

483
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,280
Because of Ching?

484
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:18,760
Why didn't you tell me
you broke up with him?

485
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:23,360
That creep, he's worried you can't
manage on your own,

486
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:25,680
he already gave me the heads up.

487
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:32,800
He said he's working for a professor abroad.

488
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:35,920
Mom, that's his dream.

489
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:38,600
He already put it off long enough for me.

490
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:43,040
I brought it up. Don't blame him.

491
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:47,640
He promised to take care of you
for the rest of his life.

492
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:50,120
That's why I let you move in with him.

493
00:26:50,760 --> 00:26:54,800
If I knew he was just like your loser father

494
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:56,600
I would never have agreed to it.

495
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:02,160
I was happy these past eight years.

496
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:07,640
From the day of my injury,

497
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:10,360
I knew Ching would leave me eventually.

498
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:14,760
I already gained eight years. I'm content.

499
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:20,120
Only you would still defend him.

500
00:27:24,640 --> 00:27:28,880
It's entirely that creep's fault

501
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:31,200
for doing this to you.

502
00:27:33,120 --> 00:27:33,880
(One week before the incident)

503
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,680
I don't want any more treatments.

504
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,360
The world is so unfair.

505
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:39,840
Mom, we work so hard.

506
00:27:40,120 --> 00:27:41,320
What about Ngai Ka-yan?

507
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:43,760
For what he did to hurt other people,
he's doing better and better.

508
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,920
Ngai Ka-yan? My boss Jarvis?

509
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:51,560
I just found out my injury
was not an accident.

510
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:54,760
It was one of Ngai Ka-yan's pranks
that paralyzed me.

511
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:59,040
Ngai Ka-yan, you scumbag...

512
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:02,640
Forget it, Mom! He's dead.

513
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:04,240
He got his retribution.

514
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:07,120
You and I will always have each other.

515
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:09,880
It's good that your Dad and Ching are gone.

516
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:13,200
Let's live our lives well, OK?

517
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:16,560
What a silly girl!

518
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:19,880
I'm glad I still have you.

519
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:23,360
Why don't you move back home with me?

520
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:26,120
Your legs have inflammation.

521
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,640
They just got better this past year
after I moved out.

522
00:28:28,720 --> 00:28:30,960
You want a relapse and make me worry?

523
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:34,760
I'm worried about you living
out there alone.

524
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:36,560
You're not worried I'll have a heart attack?

525
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:39,760
OK...I made up my mind.

526
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:41,680
You're sleeping over tonight.

527
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:45,760
Why are you irritable? That's so unlike you.

528
00:28:56,680 --> 00:29:02,160
Because you won't listen to me.

529
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:06,640
You think I'm still young?

530
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:08,960
How much longer can I work?

531
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:12,360
If only I could still cook for you

532
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:17,840
and take care of my precious daughter
one day at a time,

533
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:22,040
I'll be perfectly content.

534
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,480
But the dialysis machine is at home.

535
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:30,040
We'll go get it right after dinner.

536
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:33,360
Call the landlord tomorrow
and terminate your lease.

537
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:37,680
OK...whatever you say.

538
00:29:52,840 --> 00:29:56,600
What's wrong? Not used to sleeping here
after so long?

539
00:29:56,840 --> 00:29:59,680
No, I keep having nightmares.

540
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:01,200
What did you dream of?

541
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:05,840
I was back in the playground in high school.

542
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:08,520
I could still walk and run

543
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:11,320
and I was running around with my classmates.

544
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:15,640
Suddenly, a pair of hands reached out
from underground and grabbed my legs

545
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:16,480
and won't let me go.

546
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:20,760
I screamed for help and people ignored me.

547
00:30:21,080 --> 00:30:23,600
Were those Jarvis' hands?

548
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:27,600
I thought so. But I couldn't see.

549
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:32,640
I hope he's not giving me nightmares
now that he's dead.

550
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:36,960
Think nothing of it.

551
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:42,000
A creep like him shooting videos of
pranks he pulled on people,

552
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:47,320
will get himself killed eventually
even if it didn't happen this time.

553
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:53,120
What are you looking at? It's late.

554
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:54,720
Each time I can't sleep,

555
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:58,840
I'd bring out the photo album
and look at old photos

556
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:04,040
to see how hard I worked

557
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:10,000
to raise my precious daughter.

558
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:14,400
If I survived then,

559
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:18,240
all the unhappy things seem trivial.

560
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:23,680
Thanks, Mom!

561
00:31:26,320 --> 00:31:31,520
I'm sorry, if I didn't end up like this,

562
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:34,600
your life could have been wonderful.

563
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:38,960
It's wonderful enough.

564
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:40,600
See?

565
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:48,160
Oops...I guess it's not as
wonderful as I have imagined.

566
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:53,880
It's OK, let you and your future husband
fill in the rest.

567
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:59,640
Let's not wait. Let's fill it up now.

568
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:15,560
If Director Tsui doesn't want to run it,

569
00:32:15,760 --> 00:32:17,080
let's clear out Jarvis' office...

570
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:19,520
No! Nobody touches Jarvis' things.

571
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:24,160
Wendy, he's gone.

572
00:32:24,520 --> 00:32:25,840
Even if he was your idol...

573
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:28,800
He's not my idol, he's the hero
who saved my life.

574
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:30,880
When I was in high school,

575
00:32:31,080 --> 00:32:33,120
I was bullied every day.

576
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:40,640
Are you OK? Did we hit you?

577
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:43,360
You have such a good figure,
why didn't you dodge?

578
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:45,520
She meant to but couldn't do it in time.

579
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:47,120
All the nutrients went over there,

580
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:49,920
making them so heavy, it'll take longer.

581
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:51,920
Oh dear, she'll become a moron.

582
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:54,400
She may have a lot of shortcomings,
but she has one virtue.

583
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:56,800
She can send out sexual vibes

584
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:58,720
so the boys will block the ball for her.

585
00:32:58,800 --> 00:33:00,160
That's beyond your comprehension.

586
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:01,280
Let's play ball.

587
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:03,760
Sorry to interrupt.

588
00:33:06,760 --> 00:33:09,120
All I could do back then was cry.

589
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:13,320
The only thing that cheered me up
was when Jarvis posted new videos.

590
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:16,520
Then one time, in one of the videos

591
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:18,400
I saw the boy whom I hated most.

592
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:22,840
1...2...3... pull!

593
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:30,680
I was beaming when classmates
laughed at him.

594
00:33:31,320 --> 00:33:34,800
Since that day, Jarvis became my hero.

595
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:36,320
I joined the online channel

596
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:39,040
so I can become Robin to Jarvis' Batman.

597
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:43,520
But Batman wouldn't want Robin
to go on like this.

598
00:33:44,040 --> 00:33:46,000
What would he want Robin to do?

599
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:49,360
Pull yourself together
and do something meaningful.

600
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:52,960
For example, finish what he started...

601
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:55,520
Can I?

602
00:33:59,280 --> 00:34:01,360
Wendy! Are you Wendy?

603
00:34:02,080 --> 00:34:04,360
I've been following you. Can we have a word?

604
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:05,520
I don't know you.

605
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:06,640
I have nothing to say to you.

606
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:09,200
I have something that
you'll be very interested in.

607
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,280
Hey...
Wendy...

608
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:11,880
Stop it! She said she doesn't know you.

609
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:13,840
No, Wendy! You'll want to see this.

610
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:16,640
Wendy...what are you doing? Wendy!

611
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:17,360
(One week later)

612
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:23,280
Honey, there's no point filling up
the photo album on purpose.

613
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:25,360
Everything is paid for. You must show up.

614
00:34:25,640 --> 00:34:28,240
Still. We didn't have to dress up like this.

615
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:29,760
You said you wanted more memories.

616
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:32,880
OK, let me choose the last outfit.

617
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:36,960
Mom, this is an extreme challenge.

618
00:34:37,160 --> 00:34:39,920
A qipao is impossible to carry.

619
00:34:41,200 --> 00:34:46,480
Your grandma and I once went to a studio
and took pictures in a qipao.

620
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:48,880
Now that we have this chance,

621
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:50,880
I'd like to do the same.

622
00:34:51,200 --> 00:34:53,840
When you have a daughter,

623
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:56,880
you must bring her to a studio
and take pictures in a qipao.

624
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:02,320
Even if I had son, I'd force him to come

625
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:07,640
and the three of us can take pictures.

626
00:35:08,200 --> 00:35:10,320
I can't wait for that day.

627
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:17,280
Sin? Sin!

628
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:18,800
What's wrong?

629
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:21,160
Get us an ambulance! Please...

630
00:35:21,240 --> 00:35:22,800
Sin...
Call for an ambulance...

631
00:35:22,880 --> 00:35:24,560
Sin...

632
00:35:33,160 --> 00:35:37,160
Doctor, why did my daughter pass out?

633
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:41,720
The ostomy of Miss Lok's tube for dialysis
has been infected.

634
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,200
The inflammation gave her a fever,

635
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,760
she passed out because
she didn't have enough rest.

636
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:47,680
I'll prescribe antibiotics and antipyretics
for her and she'll be fine.

637
00:35:47,760 --> 00:35:49,360
Thank you, Doctor.

638
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:51,680
She's in the queue for a kidney transplant,

639
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:54,120
be careful and make sure her condition
doesn't deteriorate.

640
00:35:55,680 --> 00:35:56,960
Thank you.

641
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:04,240
Why didn't you tell me you need
a kidney transplant?

642
00:36:05,040 --> 00:36:07,040
You didn't want to become a burden to me?

643
00:36:08,560 --> 00:36:12,400
That's why you insisted on getting
the photo shoot.

644
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:17,920
Hiu-sin! Auntie Ching!

645
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:18,760
Dr. Yuen!

646
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:21,920
Dr. Yuen, I'm glad to see you.

647
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:26,960
From now on, please keep me posted
of my daughter's condition.

648
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:30,560
She's so willful, not until she passed out,

649
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:32,560
she didn't tell me she needed
a kidney transplant.

650
00:36:32,640 --> 00:36:33,280
Mom!

651
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,240
Dr. Yuen, why are you here?

652
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,520
I have news for you.

653
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:39,160
What is it?

654
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:40,320
It's good news.

655
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:44,000
I told Hiu-sin about a new technology
in Switzerland.

656
00:36:44,240 --> 00:36:45,760
I just heard back from them,

657
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:48,160
they accepted Hiu-sin for their
clinical trial.

658
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:53,720
What new technology?

659
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:57,120
Implanting electrodes that contain
spinal fluid into the brain

660
00:36:57,320 --> 00:37:00,640
to reconnect the paralyzed patient's
brain and lower body.

661
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:05,280
In short, if it's successful,

662
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:07,240
Hiu-sin can walk again.

663
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:13,760
Oh dear, if you won't tell me the bad news,

664
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:15,760
at least tell me the good news.

665
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:17,760
Since I don't know if they'll accept
my application,

666
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:19,840
I didn't want to get excited over nothing.

667
00:37:19,960 --> 00:37:26,400
This piece of news is making my adrenaline
or something...

668
00:37:26,520 --> 00:37:29,920
I don't know...I can't describe
my excitement.

669
00:37:30,160 --> 00:37:30,800
Mom!

670
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:33,440
Will you go with me?

671
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:37,160
You told me before not to think too much.

672
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:41,040
You may not get used to living in Europe,

673
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:44,120
but if we don't go now,

674
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:47,200
there might not be another chance.

675
00:37:52,160 --> 00:37:53,520
I will.

676
00:37:55,680 --> 00:37:58,160
I'll definitely go with you.

677
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:03,760
I don't have time for crazy fans.

678
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:06,560
Don't make me block...

679
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:10,400
Don't you want to know who held
a grudge against Jarvis?

680
00:38:12,240 --> 00:38:13,280
Who are you?

681
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:16,640
I'm Jason, a diehard fan of yours
and Jarvis'.

682
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:17,920
Why should I believe you?

683
00:38:18,240 --> 00:38:20,400
I'm a student at Jarvis' alma mater.

684
00:38:21,200 --> 00:38:22,320
The day before he died,

685
00:38:22,560 --> 00:38:25,280
I recorded his argument with someone
at the school.

686
00:38:26,120 --> 00:38:27,040
Enjoy.

687
00:38:27,640 --> 00:38:31,040
I thought you wanted to discuss
the fundraiser.

688
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:33,720
I didn't know you were a fellow alumnus.

689
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:36,000
Did you say the Alumni Association is here?

690
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:40,560
I attended all the functions.
How come I never saw you?

691
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:41,840
You haven't been back in a long time?

692
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:43,120
I don't remember.

693
00:38:44,880 --> 00:38:46,480
This place hasn't changed much.

694
00:38:46,760 --> 00:38:49,040
The teachers who taught us are gone.

695
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:50,960
Only Miss Ho is left.

696
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:53,240
When I had the accident at school,

697
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:55,120
Miss Ho has been a great help.

698
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:57,680
How sad! You have been paralyzed since
high school?

699
00:38:58,240 --> 00:39:01,200
Before the accident, I was on the
school football team.

700
00:39:01,760 --> 00:39:03,440
One day, I was practicing by myself.

701
00:39:03,840 --> 00:39:08,480
I kicked a football tied to a fishing line,

702
00:39:08,720 --> 00:39:12,320
I landed on my back and became like this.

703
00:39:14,200 --> 00:39:18,080
You hooked the football to a fishing line.

704
00:39:19,400 --> 00:39:20,560
That was you?

705
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,280
You knew all along?

706
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:25,920
I found out after I met you.

707
00:39:26,240 --> 00:39:28,880
To me, I'm not seeking any justice.

708
00:39:30,240 --> 00:39:32,760
I don't know what you intend to do
with the Static Apnea Challenge,

709
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:35,360
I only want you to cancel the prank.

710
00:39:35,600 --> 00:39:38,240
I don't want anyone else to get hurt.

711
00:39:38,560 --> 00:39:39,920
Stick to your original intention...

712
00:39:40,640 --> 00:39:42,480
fundraising.

713
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:47,240
Look Lady, your organization put in
a lot of money for this show.

714
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:48,880
Surely you want it to be effective.

715
00:39:49,360 --> 00:39:50,960
With good effects, you have viewership,

716
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:53,240
and you'll be able to raise more money.

717
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:54,640
I'd rather raise less money

718
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:56,480
than advocate this trend.

719
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:58,880
If you feel a shred of guilt
for paralyzing me...

720
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:02,880
I think you're quite mistaken.

721
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:04,560
I don't feel guilty at all.

722
00:40:04,920 --> 00:40:09,120
I have done the fishing line football
at least a dozen times,

723
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:11,360
no one else was paralyzed like you.

724
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:13,600
Rather than blame me for
having gone too far,

725
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:15,040
blame your own rotten luck.

726
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:17,440
You don't think you're accountable at all?

727
00:40:17,680 --> 00:40:19,520
Even if you survived that fall,

728
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:23,440
if you were destined to be paralyzed,
you still couldn't have dodged it.

729
00:40:23,720 --> 00:40:25,520
How could you argue in all righteousness?

730
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:27,360
Because I'm the victim here.

731
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:29,600
Why can't you look at this from
my perspective?

732
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:32,640
I came up with these pranks
because I want recognition.

733
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:35,760
But everyone thought you had an accident.

734
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:41,840
It took you years to find out
I pulled a prank on you.

735
00:40:42,200 --> 00:40:45,440
Did you realize that was the biggest insult
to an artist?

736
00:40:46,280 --> 00:40:47,440
You're out of your mind.

737
00:40:47,640 --> 00:40:49,280
I'm not talking to a lunatic

738
00:40:58,280 --> 00:40:59,440
Yes!

739
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:01,360
You're crazy!

740
00:41:03,080 --> 00:41:05,680
You simply don't understand the meaning
of these pranks to me.

741
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:08,400
You're only fixated on how I hurt people.

742
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:10,080
Wake up!

743
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:12,880
People get hurt in accidents every day.

744
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:16,200
Should we just stay home and do nothing?

745
00:41:16,440 --> 00:41:18,200
That would be no different from
being paralyzed.

746
00:41:20,080 --> 00:41:22,560
The essence of pulling pranks on others

747
00:41:22,640 --> 00:41:24,200
is to make use of someone's misfortune

748
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:26,400
in exchange for laughter.

749
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:29,160
That's why only if I keep

750
00:41:29,560 --> 00:41:31,600
pulling pranks on people without end,

751
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:36,480
will I be able to live up to the past
eight years you have been paralyzed.

752
00:41:47,640 --> 00:41:50,000
Mom, how nice of you to pick me up
from work.

753
00:41:50,240 --> 00:41:51,920
We're getting on the plane tomorrow night.

754
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:54,000
I don't know if the food overseas
is any good.

755
00:41:54,120 --> 00:41:57,240
That's why we should have a feast tonight.

756
00:41:57,520 --> 00:41:59,920
I was wondering about your relationship
with Jarvis.

757
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:02,080
Turns out you're Auntie Ching's daughter.

758
00:42:02,240 --> 00:42:05,280
Helen, there are still transition documents
you haven't signed.

759
00:42:05,400 --> 00:42:07,600
Go get your work done.

760
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:11,280
Since I forgot to buy a neck pillow,
I'll go get it now.

761
00:42:11,440 --> 00:42:14,240
When you're done, we'll meet back home, OK?

762
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:15,120
Yes!

763
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:38,280
You're crazy!

764
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:42,000
You simply don't understand the meaning
of these pranks to me.

765
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:44,560
You must have killed Jarvis!
